WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.679 --> 00:00:06.640
Many have wanted to compare him to DONALD
TRUMP, but...

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.190
Poor old Donald Trump wishes he looked like
Berlusconi!

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:15.080
We could say that Berlusconi started from
nothing and conquered absolute power like

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.019
almost no one else in history.

00:00:17.019 --> 00:00:19.300
He not only conquered political power in Italy.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.510
He also amassed business power... and media
power.

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:25.690
If power corrupts, absolute power corrupts
absolutely.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:29.949
And Berlusconi's life has many shadows...
but also many highlights!

00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:33.500
To begin with, there is something that we
have to recognize about this man and it’s

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.620
something that, frankly, is enviable....

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:36.620
HIS ENERGY!

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:37.620
Think about it...

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:41.680
Berlusconi died on 12 June at the age of 86:
he was an old man.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:53.739
Well, last year he appeared on TIKTOK with
this video.

00:00:53.739 --> 00:00:56.300
We are not going to go into the message of
the video.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:01.390
What I want to emphasize is that the man you
see was 85 years old at the time when this

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:02.550
recording was made...

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:07.020
when he was running again in an election...
in which he had a real chance of winning!

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.159
I don't know about you, but...

00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:12.200
I wish I could reach the age of 85 with that
kind of energy.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.020
That said, are we going to praise Berlusconi
in this video?

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:20.090
Of course not!

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:24.689
To speak of Berlusconi is to speak of corruption,
tailor-made laws and a political legacy that

00:01:24.689 --> 00:01:26.369
is mediocre to say the least.

00:01:26.369 --> 00:01:30.759
We could say that a good number of the problems
Italy suffers from – and they are not few

00:01:30.759 --> 00:01:31.990
– are his fault.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:35.550
I suppose that most of the obituaries you
read out there will also mention Berlusconi's

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:39.159
many sex scandals and his bunga bunga parties...

00:01:39.159 --> 00:01:43.310
We are going to leave all that aside because
we are going to focus on two things: the political

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.270
and business profile of this man.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:48.860
And, believe me, those two aspects alone would
be enough to make a movie.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:49.860
In fact...

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.450
there is already a Berlusconi biopic and it
is a masterpiece: LORO, by Paolo Sorrentino.

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:55.479
Highly recommended.

00:01:55.479 --> 00:01:59.289
For better or worse, Berlusconi has defined
what Italy is today, but not only that!

00:01:59.289 --> 00:02:03.480
He also brought about a revolution in the
media throughout much of Europe.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.020
That said, why does everyone know Berlusconi’s
name?

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:07.310
What is his political legacy?

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.940
Why do we say he has been revolutionary in
the business world?

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:13.129
Today we are going to answer these questions,
but first... let's take a look at a bit of

00:02:13.129 --> 00:02:25.160
history.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:28.810
The first difference between Berlusconi and
Donald Trump is their birth.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:32.810
While Trump was born into a family that was
already immensely wealthy, Berlusconi was

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:35.070
born into a middle-class family in Milan.

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:37.720
Normal parents, normal education and normal
life.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:41.459
However, Berlusconi had something special:
he was fascinated by show business and was

00:02:41.459 --> 00:02:43.459
the best salesman you could find.

00:02:43.459 --> 00:02:46.180
In fact, Berlusconi's beginnings were... as
a singer!

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:47.180
That’s right.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.870
Berlusconi started his career as a crooner
who entertained parties on cruise ships and

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:51.870
the like.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:55.209
Not surprisingly, that also launched his fame
as a heartthrob, but, as we said...

00:02:55.209 --> 00:03:00.790
We are not going to focus on anyone's sex
life because we are a serious channel!

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:06.019
The fact is that by entertaining the Milanese
by night, Berlusconi made the contacts to

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:09.090
start his first big business project: MILANO
DUE.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:12.299
A mega-development of 4,000 homes that was
an economic success.

00:03:12.299 --> 00:03:13.400
But make no mistake!

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.581
What Berlusconi was really interested in was
not the real estate market but... the media!

00:03:17.581 --> 00:03:18.581
In fact, Berlusconi's doctoral thesis was
precisely about the advertising business in

00:03:18.581 --> 00:03:19.581
the media – by the way, his thesis gained
a summa cum laude...

00:03:19.581 --> 00:03:22.520
In fact, in these early years of his career
we have to recognize one thing: he was a visionary.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:27.730
We are about to find out exactly how.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:31.790
(THE GODFATHER...

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.840
OF PRIVATE TV)

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:38.730
If you are watching this video from outside
Europe you might be surprised, but... there

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:41.900
was a time when private TV channels were banned
in most of Europe.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:44.489
And no, we are not talking about Eastern Europe!

00:03:44.489 --> 00:03:48.549
In the 1970s, television in Italy – and
in other countries like Spain – was a state-owned

00:03:48.549 --> 00:03:49.549
monopoly.

00:03:49.549 --> 00:03:53.959
That is, if you turned on the TV you only
had the channels of RAI, that is, the Italian

00:03:53.959 --> 00:03:55.239
state-owned television corporation.

00:03:55.239 --> 00:03:59.980
To give you an idea, in 1973, the Italian
government issued a decree prohibiting any

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:02.510
attempt to set up a private television station.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:07.400
In fact, they not only had a monopoly on television
but also on television ADVERTISING.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.900
And that was a very, very lucrative business.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:13.879
Berlusconi was perfectly aware of this and,
therefore, his goal was to end this monopoly

00:04:13.879 --> 00:04:16.820
in order to have his own national television
network.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:18.870
The question is, how did he do it?

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:21.190
Well, pay attention, because this story is
worthy of...

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:22.190
A VisualPolitik video!

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:26.260
The first question we have to ask ourselves
is why was TV a monopoly?

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:29.270
Well, because of the radio spectrum.

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:35.690
At that time there was no digital television,
let alone the internet.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:39.220
Television was broadcast by radio frequency
and the radio spectrum is limited.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:42.940
In other words: there are not infinite frequencies
for everyone who wants to broadcast TV.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:43.940
However...

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:48.400
around that time, a new technology for broadcasting
television emerged.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:53.160
Cable TV offered enough space to broadcast
multiple TV channels.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.160
The problem?

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.449
Not all homes in Italy were ready to receive
it...

00:04:56.449 --> 00:05:00.570
Except for the homes of Milano DUE that is!

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:07.440
Exactly: Berlusconi arranged for his 4,000-home
development to have cable TV.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:12.150
After a long legal battle, the Italian Constitutional
Court allowed the creation of private TV stations

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:16.500
broadcasting on cable... as long as they did
so only at the local level.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:20.200
Well, Berlusconi had 4,000 households that
could become viewers of his own television

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.200
content.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.720
This is how TELEMILANO was born.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.820
A television station that was super local...

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:27.100
It was basically a neighborhood television
station!

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:31.810
Of course, TeleMilano was not the only local
television broadcasting on cable, but it was

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:33.470
one of the most popular because...

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:35.500
It had 4,000 captive viewers!

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.470
But wait because this is only the beginning.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:42.220
Two years later, in 1976, the Constitutional
Court ruled again on the TV issue.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:46.590
This time they allowed private TV stations
to broadcast by radio frequency as long as

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:47.780
they were only local.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:52.530
That is, you could have a TV channel in Milan,
Torino or Rome... but not a channel broadcasting

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:53.530
nationally.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:55.620
So what do you think Berlusconi did at this
point?

00:05:55.620 --> 00:06:00.410
Well, good old Silvio was dedicated to buying
up all the local TV channels in all the regions

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:01.410
of Italy.

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:04.960
In a few years, he got hold of Roma TV, Video
Veneto, TeleTorino...

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:08.760
basically, he managed to get hold of all the
private TV stations in the country.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.000
He united them into Italy's first media group.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:17.430
In 1981, all these local TV stations changed
their logos to CANALE 5.

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:23.889
And that is how Berlusconi achieved what had
seemed impossible: to end a state monopoly.

00:06:23.889 --> 00:06:27.080
Now he could compete head to head with the
RAI empire.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:31.470
Thanks to having a national TV network, Canale
5 could sign the most popular public TV presenters

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:32.470
and pundits.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:36.180
This is how the famous MIKE BONGIORNO left
the state-owned corporation for the new and

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:37.819
brand new private television company.

00:06:37.819 --> 00:06:40.040
The strategy could not have been more aggressive.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:43.370
Berlusconi wanted to storm the market and,
for that, he spared no expense.

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:47.150
He bought the most popular series in the United
States and even introduced Japanese anime

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:48.450
into Italian homes.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:53.980
To give you an idea, between 1980 and 1981
alone, Canale 5 went from a turnover of 13

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:56.889
billion lire to more than 75 billion lire.

00:06:56.889 --> 00:07:02.430
By 1987, Berlusconi's TV network already had
a 48% share of the screen time in the whole

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:06.750
country.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:10.949
In case you are not yet astonished, remember
that only 15 years earlier, private television

00:07:10.949 --> 00:07:14.000
stations in Italy were not even allowed by
law.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.310
And this is a feat we have to give Berlusconi
credit for.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:20.360
But if you thought that his business career
stops here, you are very wrong: after conquering

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:25.199
Italy, Silvio went on to conquer Europe, and
boy, did he do it!

00:07:25.199 --> 00:07:30.069
Thus was born the MEDIASET GROUP, a company
that remains today, under the name MEDIA FOR

00:07:30.069 --> 00:07:34.250
EUROPE, one of the largest media groups in
Europe.

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:40.340
Basically, this man was dedicated to buying
shares in many of the private television stations

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:42.930
that were beginning to emerge in other countries
around him.

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:44.090
And this is where we come to...

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:45.090
Spain!

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:48.070
Until 1989, private television was also banned
in Spain.

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:51.449
But in the 1990s, the government put an end
to the state monopoly.

00:07:51.449 --> 00:07:55.850
And there was Silvio, also known as "il Cavaliere",
ready to enter with TELECINCO.

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:59.729
And here we come to the darkest part of Berlusconi's
business career: debt.

00:07:59.729 --> 00:08:03.430
You don't build such a media empire in just
over 10 years without borrowing money from

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:04.900
half the world.

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:09.280
By 1994, FININVEST, which is the financial
arm of Silvio's empire, was the second most

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:11.050
indebted company in all of Italy.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:12.129
So, at that point...

00:08:12.129 --> 00:08:13.180
What do you think he did?

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:16.050
What's the next step when you've become the
lord and master of the media?

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:18.259
Well... pack up your things and leave the
company!

00:08:18.259 --> 00:08:19.259
That’s right!

00:08:19.259 --> 00:08:22.250
In 1994, Berlusconi gave up all his leadership
positions.

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:24.220
However, he kept all the shares in his empire.

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:28.000
Keep this fact in mind because it is important
for the next phase of the story.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.000
But...

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.000
Where did Berlusconi go?

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:36.839
Well, we are going to look at that right now.

00:08:36.839 --> 00:08:43.250
(THE POLITICAL CONQUEST)

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:45.450
Italian politics is really crazy!

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:49.010
It doesn't matter at which point in time you
are hearing this... it applies to any period

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:50.010
in history.

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:53.150
In this country, prime ministers last on average
2.5 years.

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:57.160
If you study Italian politics you will find:
conspiracies carried out by secret lodges,

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:59.760
state terrorism and, of course, mafias of
all types.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.690
There was only one constant: CHRISTIAN DEMOCRACY.

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:05.890
We are talking about a center-right political
party that dominated the country throughout

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:07.250
the Cold War era.

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:11.740
However... in 1994, Christian Democracy was
dissolved due to a spiral of corruption scandals

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:13.700
worthy of a banana republic.

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:16.670
The right was orphaned... and the left was
not convincing voters.

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:20.089
But... where there are people willing to buy,
there is someone willing to sell.

00:09:20.089 --> 00:09:22.670
And who knew how to sell better than anyone
else?

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:23.670
Exactly!

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:24.670
Silvio Berlusconi.

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:27.510
During the 1980s, he had publicly supported
the Socialist Party.

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:30.720
But now he knew that, if he wanted to win
elections, he had to switch sides.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:32.930
And that's how he created his own center-right
party.

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:33.930
Although...

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:35.839
the truth is, we could say that it was a party
without ideology.

00:09:35.839 --> 00:09:40.090
Basically, the process was as follows
What do Italians like more than pizza and

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:41.090
women?

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:42.090
Soccer!

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:43.790
And what do Italians shout when they support
their national team?

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:44.790
FORZA ITALIA!!!

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:45.790
Great!

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:46.790
Well, we already have the name of the party...

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:47.790
Ideology?

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:54.720
Well... we are for the good and against the
bad.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.010
Who wouldn’t vote for such a party?

00:09:57.010 --> 00:10:04.210
This is how, in 1994, the year of the World
Cup, Berlusconi created Forza Italia.I don't

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:09.390
need to tell you that Berlusconi won the elections
that same year.

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:10.430
And why, you may ask?

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:14.160
For three reasons: first, he had control of
the biggest television station in the country,

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:15.160
second...

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:20.580
the rest of the parties were killing each
other in internal disputes and third, we are

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:23.780
talking about one of the most charismatic
personalities ever known.

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:27.410
So this is how the most impressive political
career in Italian history began.

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:30.580
This does not mean that Silvio has always
won the elections.

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:33.120
Remember that Italian politics is chaos...

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:34.120
Even for him!

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:36.339
He has been prime minister in different interrupted
periods.

00:10:36.339 --> 00:10:40.190
Now, we can say that Berlusconi has been the
politician who has governed Italy for the

00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:42.390
longest period of time in recent history.

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:45.660
And we can also say that he has been the Prime
Minister with the most power.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:49.070
Because he not only controlled politics but
also the media.

00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:53.579
To give you an idea, according to estimates
by The Economist, in 2001, he came to control

00:10:53.579 --> 00:10:56.950
91% of the screen share of Italian TV.

00:10:56.950 --> 00:11:00.890
Think of it this way: he was the owner of
CANALE 5 and, at the same time, he dominated

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:02.030
State television.

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:11.320
Conclusion: the man who ended the TV monopoly
in the 80s ended up building another monopoly.

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:13.820
And this is where we come to the darkest part
of his life.

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:18.139
Because if power corrupts, absolute power
corrupts absolutely.

00:11:18.139 --> 00:11:20.560
And Berlusconi turned parliament into his
backyard.

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:24.880
Plain and simple he passed laws tailor-made
for him.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:29.540
For example, in 2004, Italy passed a law to
give financial aid for the purchase of digital

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:30.540
TV decoders.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:33.050
Who had the main company that sold these devices?

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:34.050
Exactly!

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:35.050
Berlusconi's family.

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:39.019
And this is just one example in a very long
list: tax amnesties, financial regulations...

00:11:39.019 --> 00:11:43.880
we could say that Silvio changed Italy to
make it fit his interests.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:49.380
But now let's go to the most important thing
of all: the general picture.

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:51.730
What political outcome does Berlusconi leave
behind?

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:52.790
Apart from corruption...

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:54.400
Has he been good for the Italians?

00:11:54.400 --> 00:12:00.019
Well, let's take a look right now.

00:12:00.019 --> 00:12:07.470
(POWER FOR POWER'S SAKE)

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:12.800
Italy's economy is even worse than its political
class... and it makes no difference when you’re

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:13.800
hearing this.

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:16.300
Actually, Italy had a very good period in
the 1980s.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:20.579
That is, when Berlusconi was building his
business empire, the country was on fire.

00:12:20.579 --> 00:12:24.070
In the early 1990s, the Italians were richer
than the British and were close to catching

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:25.269
up with the Germans.

00:12:25.269 --> 00:12:28.460
Now, however, Italy is in Europe's intensive
care unit.

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:31.610
One of the few countries that is now poorer
than it was 20 years ago.

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:32.899
And why, you may ask?

00:12:32.899 --> 00:12:36.370
We have a couple of videos where we explain
it in detail: one from VisualPolitik and one

00:12:36.370 --> 00:12:37.540
from VisualEconomik.

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:40.019
I’ll leave the link in the description.

00:12:40.019 --> 00:12:41.560
But here is a brief summary.

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:44.730
Italy has systemic problems that make it almost
impossible for it to function.

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:48.960
It has a huge and totally inefficient State,
with more than 3 million civil servants and

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:50.020
a lot of public spending.

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:51.080
But that's not all!

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:54.500
One of Italy's great weaknesses is the most
absurd bureaucracy you can imagine.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:58.670
For example, almost all the professions are
governed by regulatory colleges.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:03.190
That means that if you want to work as a journalist
or computer scientist, you need a license.

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:08.910
And getting that license is a process that
seems to be from another era.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:15.010
Well, with all these problems, Italy in the
1980s grew thanks to one thing: they were

00:13:15.010 --> 00:13:17.380
addicted to devaluation.

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:20.820
Italy devalued its currency to make its products
cheaper on the international market.

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:24.750
During the 1980s and 1990s, "Made in Italy"
was sweeping Europe.

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:28.810
In the 2000s, China joined the World Trade
Organization and Italy joined the euro.

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:33.029
Conclusion: they could not compete with the
even cheaper prices of Chinese companies...

00:13:33.029 --> 00:13:34.720
and they could not devaluate their currency
either.

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:37.529
It began a long crisis from which they have
not yet emerged.

00:13:37.529 --> 00:13:38.529
However...

00:13:38.529 --> 00:13:41.280
Silvio Berlusconi only wanted to win elections.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:42.320
His political proposal?

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:44.730
For the good and against the bad.

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:45.730
What do Italians want?

00:13:45.730 --> 00:13:49.470
To maintain the illusion that there are no
problems, nothing needs to be reformed, and

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.120
things will be fine.

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:53.089
Maintain public spending while the economy
sinks.

00:13:53.089 --> 00:13:56.529
That is what Berlusconi has always promised
and what Berlusconi has achieved.

00:13:56.529 --> 00:13:59.090
So what is the flipside of this policy?

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:06.450
Well you see, right now, Italy ranks 7th in
the world in debt to GDP and 5th in debt per

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:07.450
capita.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:10.320
In fact, today, Italy is one of the biggest
headaches in all of Europe.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:15.079
And in a way a good part of that is due to
what Berlusconi did, or rather did NOT do

00:14:15.079 --> 00:14:19.009
despite having more power than almost any
other politician.

00:14:19.009 --> 00:14:22.850
And what has Berlusconi done in recent years?

00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:25.139
Well, the truth is that he has never abandoned
politics.

00:14:25.139 --> 00:14:30.040
As we saw at the beginning, even at the age
of 84 he continued to run for election.

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:35.699
However, we can hardly find any interesting
political position... except this one.

00:14:35.699 --> 00:14:41.399
(Silvio Berlusconi: Ex-PM defends Russian
war on eve of Italian election.

00:14:41.399 --> 00:14:42.399
– BBC)

00:14:42.399 --> 00:14:43.399
Exactly!

00:14:43.399 --> 00:14:45.040
Berlusconi has been supporting Russia in the
Ukrainian war.

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:46.170
And why, you may ask?

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:47.889
Well, his argument was based on the fact that...

00:14:47.889 --> 00:14:50.920
He knew Vladimir Putin personally and they
were very good friends.

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:56.300
In this case, it seems that Berlusconi's private
life DOES affect his political positions...

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:59.000
or so it appears from photos like this one.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:00.000
Conclusion?

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.290
No one can deny that Berlusconi was a true
genius: a self-made man.

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:07.230
He managed to have more power than almost
any other man in history: he combined economic,

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:09.500
political and media power in the same person.

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:13.180
However, he used all that power in a mediocre
way, to say the least.

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:18.870
But now the questions are for you: Will we
ever see a new leader with as much power as

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:19.910
Berlusconi?

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:22.540
Are there other international leaders we could
compare with IL CAVALIERE?

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:23.540
And...

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:26.680
Would you like to reach 80-something years
of age with as much energy as Silvio?

00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:28.520
You can leave me your answer in the comments.

00:15:28.520 --> 00:15:32.470
As always, don't forget that here, on VisualPolitik,
we release new videos every week, so subscribe

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:36.240
to this channel and hit the little bell so
you don't miss any of our updates.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:38.720
If you liked this video, LIKE it and see you
in the next one.

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:40.949
All the best and see you soon.

